**Important:** These connections are the authoritative pin assignments for this wiring guide. The firmware must use the same GPIO assignments. GPIO 2 is not used by this design.

## I2C Bus (RTC + LCD)

The DS3231 real-time clock and the 16x2 LCD with its I2C backpack share a single I2C bus.

Both devices connect to the same ESP32 data and clock pins:

- **SDA:** GPIO 21
- **SCL:** GPIO 22

I2C allows multiple devices to share the same two signal wires, provided that each device has a unique address on the bus.

### I2C Addresses

| Device | Expected Address | Function |
|---|---|---|
| DS3231 RTC | `0x68` | Maintains date and time |
| 16x2 I2C LCD | `0x27` or `0x3F` | Displays clock information |

The LCD address depends on the I2C backpack installed on the module. Use an I2C scanner to determine the actual address before configuring the firmware.

### Shared Bus Diagram

```text
                 ESP32 DevKit
                +-------------+
                |             |
GPIO 21 (SDA) --+-------------+---- SDA ---- DS3231 RTC
                |             |       |
                |             |       +---- SDA ---- I2C LCD
GPIO 22 (SCL) --+-------------+---- SCL ---- DS3231 RTC
                |             |       |
                |             |       +---- SCL ---- I2C LCD
                |             |
3V3 ------------+-------------+------------ RTC VCC
VIN (5V) -------+-------------+------------ LCD VCC
GND ------------+-------------+------------ RTC GND
                |             +------------ LCD GND
                +-------------+
